-- title:
--   Per-node core of the layered node presentations at q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, $\mathcal F =$ `fieldBar q M'` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ with group $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times\bigr)$, and `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`; $j$ stands for the image of the Laurent series `jq` in these fields, and $J$ for [`ModularCurve.jqNModC (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18).
--
--   **Data and standing hypotheses.** A prime $q$ with $q=2$; a nonzero $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g\equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g\mid M'$ (the rigidity guard on the auxiliary level). A valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over the residue field of $A$, characterised by `hW` as exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`, and a chosen $s\in W$. The inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` in $\mathcal F$. A constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ on `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` with residue field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers` inducing $A$ on constants, a surjective residue map whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with reduction on $A$, together with its place map and the order-preservation axioms), and the hypothesis `hR₀` that coefficientwise reduction of Laurent series with coefficients in $A$ is computed by `R₀.residue`.
--
--   *Constants block:* an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ lying in $A$, such that the contracted ring $A\cap k_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian, and has algebraically closed residue field; `hκ` states that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0\cap A$.
--
--   *Auxiliary prime and tame parameter:* a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0\in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; an element $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$; an element $\pi_t\in A$ with $\pi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q$.
--
--   *Layer family:* a type $\iota$, intermediate fields $K_n$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, each finite-dimensional over $k_0$, with valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ cut out by $A$; a least index $n_0$ with $K_{n_0}\le K_n$ for all $n$; the cofinality hypothesis `hKcof` that every finite subset of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is contained in the image of some $K_n$; and `htame`, that every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup `A.inertiaSubgroupIn ℚ` with trivial tame character `A.tameCharacter πt τ = 1` fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise.
--
--   *Base presentation:* an intermediate field $K_b=\bot$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$, a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ cut out by $A$, and a nonzero generator $\varpi_b$ of its maximal ideal.
--
--   **The quantified objects.** With $k_0$ acting on $\mathcal F$ through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, the assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $\mathcal F/k_0$ satisfying the four *level-field* conditions: (i) $f\in F_0$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $f$ lies in (the image of) $k_0$; (ii) the subfield generated by $F_0$ and the constants $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of $\mathcal F$; (iii) $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; (iv) the linear-disjointness condition: for every intermediate field $K'$ finite over $k_0$, every family $c_i\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i=0$ forces all $a_i=0$.
--
--   Further, for every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$, every subring $B$ of $\mathcal F$ with an $A_b$-algebra structure, the hypotheses `hjR` (the image of `jq` lies in `R₀.integers`) and `hjs` (its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$), `hJK` ($J\in\mathcal F$), an element $a_0\in k_0\cap A$ whose residue satisfies $\overline{a_0}^{\,q}=s(\,\overline{j}\,)$ (the Hasse lift, where $s(\cdot)$ is `Place.evalAt` at $s$), and every finite set `nodes` of subrings of $F_0$.
--
--   **The antecedent** (a long conjunction; the groups are named here, and the content of each is given). *(W1)* $W_0$ induces $A$ on $k_0$; *(W2)* $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; *(W3)* $\pi_0$ generates its maximal ideal; *(W4)* the *centring at $s$*: for every $g\in$ `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose image lies in `R₀.integers` and which has no pole wherever $j$ has none (i.e. $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}\,j$ implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}\,g$ for all places $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $g$ lies in $F_0$, lies in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ with $\overline c = s(\overline g)$ the difference lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$; *(W5)* $W_0$ is invariant under all `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   *(B)* the affine-chart conditions on $B$: the $A_b$-algebra structure is the one induced by $K_b\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}\subseteq\mathcal F$; $B$ is contained in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by $K_b$, and every element of that compositum is a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator; $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$, and $B/(\varpi_b)$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$; $\varpi_b$ is prime in $B$; $W_0$ is the set of quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\varpi_b\nmid h$; $j\in B$; $B$ is stable under all `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$. Two *pole* clauses: there is $b\in B\cap F_0$ lying in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which induces $A$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$, and is such that every monic polynomial over $k_0$ with $A$-integral coefficients evaluated at $j$ is a unit of $V$ whenever it lies in $V$; and for every $s'\in W$ with $s'\ne s$ there is $b\in B\cap F_0$ lying in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ which induces $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfies the clause *(W4)* with $s'$ in place of $s$ and $V$ in place of $W_0$. A *Drinfeld-curve* clause: for every $(\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2)$-algebra structure on the residue field $\kappa$ of $A$ for which [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta\in$ `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\ q\ 2$ and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) with $\#C_s =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, kernel the ideal generated by $\varpi_b$, reduction-compatible on $A_b$, with every element of the target a quotient of values of $\rho$, with image characterised as the set of elements lying in the image of [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) inside the Drinfeld function field, and equivariant for `hFunctionFieldAction` under those $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ for which $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ lies in `hSubgroup q`.
--
--   *(N)* the node conditions: $\#\,$`nodes`$\,=q+1$; there is a subring $B_c$ of $F_0$, generated as a ring by the constants $k_0\cap A$ together with a finite set, which is contained in each $\mathcal O\in$ `nodes` and of which each such $\mathcal O$ is the localisation (membership in $\mathcal O$ is being a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B_c$ and $h$ a unit of $\mathcal O$ whenever it lies in $\mathcal O$); the level automorphisms permute `nodes`, and act transitively on it (for every $\zeta$ and every pair $\mathcal O,\mathcal O'$ there is $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ carrying one to the other in the sense that $f\in\mathcal O$ iff `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` $f\in\mathcal O'$); distinct nodes are separated (some common element is a non-unit in one and a unit in the other); and the covering clause: every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ inducing $A$ on $k_0$ and satisfying *(W4)* with $V$ in place of $W_0$ either contains all of $B$ or dominates some $\mathcal O\in$ `nodes` (contains $\mathcal O$, with non-units of $\mathcal O$ landing in the maximal ideal of $V$).
--
--   Finally, per node $\mathcal O\in$ `nodes`: $\mathcal O\subseteq W_0$; $\mathcal O$ is local and Noetherian; it induces $A$ on $k_0$ and its residue field is that of $A$ (for each $f\in\mathcal O$ some $x\in k_0\cap A$ makes $f-x$ a non-unit); and there are $E_0\ge 1$, a unit $v$ of $A$ in $k_0$ with $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{\,\mathrm{pwc}}v$ where $\mathrm{pwc}=$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, elements $c_x,c_y\in\mathcal O$, a unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$, an isomorphism $\iota$ of the adic completion of $\mathcal O$ with the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion of $A\cap k_0$ with parameter $\pi_0^{E_0}$, and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model such that $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$, $\iota$ carries constants to `const`, $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\,U$ and $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\,V$, $c_y$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_0$ while $c_x$ does not; the Hasse-germ clause that $J-a_0$ lies in $F_0$ and in $\mathcal O$ with $\iota$-image $w_V V^e$ for some unit $w_V$ and some $e\ge 1$; an *Igusa branch* $W_x$, a valuation subring of $F_0$ containing $\mathcal O$, inducing $A$ on $k_0$, a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, carrying an element $t$ whose reduction is transcendental (if a polynomial over $k_0$ with $A$-integral coefficients has $p(t)$ in the maximal ideal, all its coefficients do), with $c_x$ in the maximal ideal and $c_y$ not, with the reduction dictionary that for $g$ as in *(W4)* the image lies in $F_0$ and $W_x$, lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ exactly when its $R_0$-residue vanishes, and, when that residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, lies in $\mathcal O$ and is congruent there to any $c\in k_0\cap A$ with $\overline c=s(\overline g)$; and, for every other node $\mathcal O'$, an element of $\mathcal O'$ not lying in $W_x$. Together with a subring $B_x$ of $F_0$ contained in $B\cap\mathcal O$, all of whose elements have no pole wherever $j$ has none, of which $\mathcal O$ is the localisation, which generates $F_0$ as a field of fractions, which is generated by the constants $k_0\cap A$ and a finite set, and which contains an element $b$ lying in no valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ that induces $A$ on $k_0$, has $\pi_0$ in its maximal ideal, contains $j$ with all monic $A$-integral polynomial values in $j$ units, and fails to contain some element of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Granting all of the above, the following holds: for every field $\mathrm{FSS}$ over the residue field of $A$ and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ on $\mathcal F$ with residue field $\mathrm{FSS}$ such that, for $f\in F_0$, $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $f\in W_0$, there is a finite set $N$ of places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over the residue field of $A$ with
--   $$\#N=q+1,$$
--   together with: fields $\mathrm{FI}_x$ over the residue field of $A$ indexed by places $x$ of $\mathrm{FSS}$, regular prolongations $R_x$ of $A$ on $\mathcal F$ with residue field $\mathrm{FI}_x$, places $b_x$ of $\mathrm{FI}_x$; subrings $C'_l\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ contained in $A$, each a domain and a discrete valuation ring, with elements $\varpi'_l$; complete discrete valuation rings $W_{c,l}$ with elements $\pi_l$, natural numbers $E_l$ and $E_0$; sets $S(\mathrm{nd})$ of places of $\mathcal F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, subrings $\mathcal N(\mathrm{nd})$ and local Noetherian subrings $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ of $\mathcal F$, and elements $c_x(\mathrm{nd}),c_y(\mathrm{nd}),c_u(\mathrm{nd})$ of $\mathcal F$, such that all of the following hold.
--
--   *Layer constants.* $c\in C'_l$ if and only if $c\in A$ and $c$ lies in the image of $K_l$; for $d\in C'_l$, the residue of $d$ in $A$ vanishes exactly when $d\in\varpi'_lC'_l$; $C'_{n_0}\subseteq C'_l$ for all $l$; $\varpi'_{n_0}\ne 0$; every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C'_{n_0}$; each $\pi_l$ is irreducible and $E_l\ge 1$; every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup with trivial tame character fixes $\varpi'_{n_0}$; and there are $w\ge 1$ and a unit $v$ of $A$ with $(\varpi'_{n_0})^{E_0}=v\,\pi_t^{\,w}$.
--
--   *Per node $\mathrm{nd}\in N$.* There is $\mathcal O\in$ `nodes` whose elements map into $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},n_0)$, preserving non-units, such that $S(\mathrm{nd})$ is exactly the set of places $P$ of $\mathcal F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\mathcal O$ inside the valuation subring of $P$ and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ in the maximal ideal of $A$ for every non-unit $f$ of $\mathcal O$; moreover $R$-residues of elements of $\mathcal O$ lie in the valuation subring of $\mathrm{nd}$, those of non-units lie in its maximal ideal, and $\mathrm{nd}$ is the unique place of $\mathrm{FSS}$ with these two properties. The places $b_x(\mathrm{nd})$, $\mathrm{nd}$ and every $P\in S(\mathrm{nd})$ are rational. $\mathcal N(\mathrm{nd})$ consists of the elements lying in $R_x(\mathrm{nd}).\mathrm{integers}$, in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and in the valuation subring of every $P\in S(\mathrm{nd})$; and $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f\in A$ for $f\in\mathcal N(\mathrm{nd})$ and $P\in S(\mathrm{nd})$. One has the crossing relation
--   $$c_x(\mathrm{nd})\,c_y(\mathrm{nd})=(\varpi'_{n_0})^{E_0}\,c_u(\mathrm{nd}),$$
--   with the $R_x(\mathrm{nd})$-residue of $c_x(\mathrm{nd})$ zero, the order of the $R$-residue of $c_x(\mathrm{nd})$ at $\mathrm{nd}$ equal to $1$, the $R$-residue of $c_y(\mathrm{nd})$ zero, and the order of the $R_x(\mathrm{nd})$-residue of $c_y(\mathrm{nd})$ at $b_x(\mathrm{nd})$ equal to $1$. For every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup with trivial tame character, the action $g=$ [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')) τ`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) preserves $S(\mathrm{nd})$ and fixes $c_x(\mathrm{nd})$ and $c_y(\mathrm{nd})$. Every element of $\mathcal F$ is a quotient of elements of $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ for some $l$, and is also a quotient of an $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-linear combination of elements of $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},n_0)$ by a nonzero element of $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},n_0)$.
--
--   For each layer $l$: $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},n_0)\subseteq\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)\subseteq\mathcal N(\mathrm{nd})$; $S(\mathrm{nd})$ is likewise characterised by $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ (the places containing it whose evaluation sends non-units into the maximal ideal of $A$); $C'_l$ maps into $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$, each element of which is congruent to an element of $C'_l$ modulo non-units; families in $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ with coefficients linearly independent over $C'_l$ satisfy only the trivial relation; there is a subring $B_x\subseteq\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ containing $c_x(\mathrm{nd}),c_y(\mathrm{nd}),c_u(\mathrm{nd})$, of which $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ is the localisation, generated by the image of $C'_l$ together with a finite set; $c_x(\mathrm{nd}),c_y(\mathrm{nd})\in\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ and $c_u(\mathrm{nd})$ is a unit there; and there are a ring homomorphism $\sigma$ from $W_{c,l}$ to the adic completion of $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ and an isomorphism $\iota_c$ of that completion with `UVCrossingModel (Wc l) (π l ^ E l)` such that $\sigma(\pi_l)$ is the image of $\varpi'_l$ whenever the latter lies in $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$, $\iota_c\circ\sigma$ is `const`, the element $J-a_0$ lies in $\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ with $\iota_c$-image $w\,V^e$ for a unit $w$ and some $e\ge 1$, every constant from $C'_l$ lies in the image of $\sigma$, and the two branch dictionaries hold: if $f\in\mathcal N_0(\mathrm{nd},l)$ has nonzero $R_x(\mathrm{nd})$-residue of order $n$ at $b_x(\mathrm{nd})$, then $\iota_c(f)-\gamma V^n$ lies in the ideal generated by `const (π l ^ E l) (π l)` and $U$ for some unit $\gamma$ of the model; and symmetrically, if $f$ has nonzero $R$-residue of order $n$ at $\mathrm{nd}$, then $\iota_c(f)-\gamma U^n$ lies in the ideal generated by `const (π l ^ E l) (π l)` and $V$.
--
--   *Global clauses.* The sets $S(\mathrm{nd})$, $\mathrm{nd}\in N$, are pairwise disjoint. For $\mathrm{nd}\in N$, $P\in S(\mathrm{nd})$ and $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with no pole wherever $j$ has none and with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and for every $a\in A$ with $\overline a=s(\overline f)$, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the image of $f$ minus $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$. For every $\zeta'$ and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ there is a map $\tau_N$ on places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ preserving $N$ with $(\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta'\,\gamma)\cdot P\in S(\mathrm{nd})$ iff $P\in S(\tau_N\mathrm{nd})$, and with $R_x(\tau_N\mathrm{nd}).\mathrm{integers}$ the preimage of $R_x(\mathrm{nd}).\mathrm{integers}$ under that automorphism. For every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the residual automorphism `R.resAut τ` maps $N$ into $N$ and `RegularProlongation.smulDisc τ (S nd) = S (R.resAut τ hτ • nd)`. For $\mathrm{nd}\in N$, the image of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ lies in $R_x(\mathrm{nd}).\mathrm{integers}$, and there is a ring homomorphism $j_{\mathrm{nd}}$ from `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` to $\mathrm{FI}_{\mathrm{nd}}$ computing $R_x(\mathrm{nd})$-residues of images of elements of $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ from their $R_0$-residues, and pulling back the valuation subring of $b_x(\mathrm{nd})$ to that of $s$. Finally, for distinct $x,x'\in N$ there is $g$ lying in both $\mathcal N_0(x,n_0)$ and $\mathcal N_0(x',n_0)$ which is $c_x(x)$ times a unit of $\mathcal N_0(x,n_0)$ and a unit of $\mathcal N_0(x',n_0)$.
--
--   This is the per-node core of the layered node presentation of the semistable model of the modular curve at a supersingular point in the case $q=2$, at a rigid auxiliary level: from a level-field model $(F_0,W_0)$ with an affine chart $B$, node rings and separated Igusa branches, it produces, for any regular prolongation $R$ realising $W_0$, the $q+1$ nodal places with their residue discs, branch prolongations, layered local rings and crossing-model normal forms $xy=(\varpi')^{E_0}u$, together with the Hasse germ of $J-a_0$ along one branch. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep_of_eq_two_of_dvd), which assembles the node presentations of the special fibre.
